# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-15). L §5.16: "mean(e) over the paths prints the mean with its standard error s/√N ...
# The sums under them aren't values at a key, so the 4 096-digit cap doesn't reach them (§7.1)". y is big (4 095 nines)
# on every path: the sum over 20 paths passes 4 096 digits, the mean, big carried through, doesn't, so the line prints
# it (refused RUN-DIGITS on 2.0). A value at a key still is capped: big * hundred (L §7.1, RUN-DIGITS).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input big: num
input mu: num
input sd: num
input t0: date
input hundred: num
def d: dist = normal(mu, sd) to 1e-9 at t0
def y: num = big + d * 0 at t0

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  big = 
  mu = 0
  sd = 1
  t0 = 2026-01-01
  hundred = 100

ask q: mean(y) paths 20 seed 1
ask r: big * hundred
=== expect
q: 999 999 999 ...
  cut 2026-01-01
r: refused: RUN-DIGITS a value passes 4 096 digits; round where the law rounds
  cut 2026-01-01
